menu "MQTT over HyperDHT"

config MQTT_P2P_NODE
    string "Network name, or a node's public key in hex"
    default "boat-mqtt"
    help
        A network name: the device looks up BLAKE2b-256(name) on HyperDHT and
        connects to one of the nodes announced there (packages/boat-mqtt-node).
        64 hex characters: that node only.

config MQTT_P2P_INTERVAL
    int "Seconds between telemetry messages"
    default 5

config MQTT_P2P_SIGN
    bool "Sign telemetry with the device key"
    default y
    help
        Each telemetry message carries the device's Ed25519 signature over the
        topic, a sequence number and the payload (hdht_mqtt_sign), so apps can
        check it whatever node or bridge it came through.

endmenu
